    "narrative": "The Austin Waves feature a high-upside offensive slate today, headlined by the dual-threat production of **Kyle Tucker** (82.82) and **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88). Both benefit significantly from favorable matchups against Zack Littell and Jack Kochanowicz, respectively; **Kyle Tucker** maintains an elite base projection, while **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s score is buoyed by an 18% boost due to SP skill factors and a dynamic platoon advantage. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.73) and **Jackson Merrill** (68.69) are also vital components of our scoring, as both leverage favorable batting order positions and dynamic platoon edges to maximize their efficiency scores. The emphasis on speed remains a focal point, as we are looking to capitalize on **Nasim Nunez** (56.97) and **Brady House** (59.63) against Shane Baz, whose slow delivery profile provides a clear lane for stolen base opportunities.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Coby Mayo** (51.96), who narrowly missed the cut behind **Josh Jung** (59.79). While **Coby Mayo** benefits from the same SP skill tailwinds as the rest of the lineup, his projected spot at the bottom of the order and a negative platoon split against right-handed pitching ultimately forced the optimizer to favor **Josh Jung**\u2019s utility role. Risk management remains critical today as all scores are derived from \"Lineup Pending\" status; if **Drake Baldwin** or **Sam Antonacci** slide down their respective batting orders, their sub-55 scores will drop precipitously toward the \"Below Floor\" category. We are monitoring these lineups closely, particularly for **Drake Baldwin**, whose score is already suppressed by a difficult matchup against the 2.92 xERA of Connelly Early.",
